# Terraform local state, plans, and vars — never commit these.
#
# NOT in this list, deliberately: `.terraform.lock.hcl`. It was, and that was a
# mistake — a dependency lock is not state. It is this module's `pnpm-lock.yaml`,
# and HashiCorp's own guidance is to commit it. Without it `versions.tf`'s `~>`
# constraints float, so CI resolved a different provider build on every run with
# nothing verifying the download. It is committed, and regenerated with
# `terraform providers lock -platform=...` for the four platforms README.md's
# "Notes and gotchas" lists. Read that note before changing the platform list —
# what the list buys is not that `init` fails without it, because it does not.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars
crash.log
